souran (5.0.0) resolute; urgency=low

  * Security: removed a plaintext sudo password that was embedded in six
    source files and had already reached git history. Every call site now
    uses sudo -n; the credential bought nothing because every unit runs
    unprivileged.
  * Security: added token authentication to the whole control plane. A
    root-or-service-owned 0600 token is stored outside the source tree,
    compared in constant time, and required for every control API route
    except the health and docs paths. Loopback callers stay exempt so the
    watchdog and test suites keep working.
  * Packaging: first release as a .deb. unbound is compiled from the
    vendored source during the build, so the shipped resolver is built
    from source on the target rather than copied in as a binary.
  * Packaging: TLS private keys and all *.bak / pre-* config snapshots are
    excluded from the payload. A distributable package must not ship the
    host's live private keys.

 -- Hermes Agent <souran@sitet.top>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0100

souran (4.3.6) resolute; urgency=low

  * Fixed the ground-truth oracle so MX and TXT answers are really
    verified rather than assumed.
  * Fixed truncated TXT replies corrupting the question section.
  * Added a systemd unit for the ops sidecar; 19 API routes had been dead.

 -- Hermes Agent <souran@sitet.top>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 18:56:00 +0100

souran (4.3.5) resolute; urgency=low

  * Closed unauthenticated remote code execution on the sidecar /api/exec
    endpoint, which accepted an arbitrary shell string on a
    LAN-reachable port.

